Z||000000||Steelhead||06-05-2001||02:12 PM||||First let me say that I'm brand new here and that I don't have a Fiero, but I do have a Jeep with the Iron Duke motor in it so I though I ought to go to the experts with my questions.I have been given conflicting information about Iron Duke bell housing bolt patterns I have been told that the Iron duke has the same bell housing bolt pattern as the small block chevy I have also been told that only the Iron Duke used in Jeeps have the small block chevy bell housing bolt pattern.Can some one here tell me which is correct?||||reg||1
Z||000001||elfiero||06-05-2001||02:37 PM||||1.What year is the jeep?<BR>2.Do you know if the motor is original?<BR>In the '70s they did use a 4cyl. that was a<BR>decendent of the chevyII motor-this will have<BR>a SBC bellhousing.It did use a crossflow head<BR>so it is esentially a "iron duke".Or the later engines used the current "FWD"bellhousing design.You can tell by looking at the top two bolts in the pattern-are they right at the top or are they<BR>a few inches down and does the bell housing<BR>come to a point?if so,it is SBC.<P>||||reg||6
